"'''The Supervisor'''" was a massive [[droid]]<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|the-supervisor|The Supervisor}}</ref> in charge of the [[At Attin's government|government]] of the [[planet]] of [[At Attin]]. Located in the [[Supervisor's Tower]], he controlled both the entire planet’s power supply and security systems along with its [[droid]]s.<ref name="Good Guys" /> He<ref name="Skeleton Crew Explained" /> had an [[Office of the Supervisor|office]] where [[Fara]] served as an [[Undersecretary]].<ref name="Astrogation Problem">{{SkeletonCrew|Very Interesting, As an Astrogation Problem}}</ref>

==Biography==
After four [[Youngling|children]] named [[Wim]], [[Neel]], [[Fern]], and [[KB]] found an [[Onyx Cinder|old starship]] buried in At Attin's [[Forest|woods]] outside their city and got lost in space when they accidentally activated it, the Supervisor was reached out to by the [[parent]]s of the kids so they could see how to track them down, but the Supervisor dispatched a [[droid]] to inform the worried adults that because their children had crossed the [[Barrier]] they wouldn't risk sending a ship nor contact the [[Galactic Republic]] to help locate the kids, much to the dismay of the parents, leading Fara to announce her intentions to request an immediate audience with the Supervisor to find their [[Gender|sons]] and daughters.<ref name="Astrogation Problem" />

Over time, [[Wendle]] became convinced that the Supervisor wasn't going to do anything to recover the kids and began conspiring with the other parents to go behind their back and launch a communication buoy to instruct the children on how to return home.<ref name="Pirates">{{SkeletonCrew|You Have a Lot to Learn About Pirates}}</ref>

The Supervisor later made a public announcement to all of At Attin, announcing the imminent arrival of a Republic Emissary and declared all non-essential work to be suspended until offloading was complete. Unbeknownst to everyone but the Skeleton Crew, the alleged Emissary was the [[pirate]] [[Jod Na Nawood]], who had commandeered the ''Onyx Cinder'' as part of a plan to plunder At Attin's wealth. Na Nawood would then demand a meeting with the Supervisor for aiding on communicating with his pirate [[frigate]] beyond the Barrier.<ref name="Trouble">{{SkeletonCrew|We're Gonna Be In So Much Trouble}}</ref>

When Fern, Fara and Jod met the Supervisor, he asked if it was Fara, one of his most dedicated citizens, and revealed to them he was familiar with the Undersecretary and had been watching over her and Fern with great interest, and was pleased about Fern's safe return. Jod asked if they were ruled by a droid.<ref name="Good Guys">{{SkeletonCrew|The Real Good Guys}}</ref>

The Supervisor turned his attention to Jod and asked him to introduce himself. Jod claimed to be an Emissary for the Republic and a Jedi. He used [[the Force]] to levitate his lightsaber. The Supervisor greeted him and admitted that he was beginning to doubt whether an Emissary would visit their humble [[At Attin Mint]] again, since none had in a long time. Jod claimed that the [[Galactic Republic]] had been preoccupied with thwarting numerous "evil schemes." The Supervisor remarked that the galaxy was dangerously unstable.<ref name="Good Guys" />

Jod then started to tell the Supervisor that he needed to contact his second ship, prompting Fara to ask why his second ship didn't simply land as his first one had. Jod asserted his authority by telling her that she needed to obey him as Republic Emissary. The Supervisor concurred that strict obedience to authority had kept At Attin running smoothly for generations. The Supervisor then gave Jod permission for his second ship to land, if he could clear up one tiny detail. The Supervisor revealed that the last message that they received from the Republic was that [[Order 66|all Jedi were traitors]]. He then asked Jod which he was lying about, being an Emissary or a Jedi.<ref name="Good Guys" />

[[File:DestroyingTheSupervisor-TheRealGoodGuys.png|thumb|left|300px|Jod Na Nawood stabs the supervisor with a lightsaber.]]
With Jod unable to answer, Fern shouted out that Jod was really a [[pirate]] trying to invade the mint. The Supervisor stated he had suspected that and ordered the [[safety droid]]s to arrest the imposter. When Jod looked at the Supervisor's photoreceptor, he asked what he was doing. Jod then stabbed the Supervisor with his [[Unidentified lightsaber (Lanupa)|lightsaber]], the Supervisor then sputtered, "Must- Protect- The- Mint" and deactivated.<ref name="Good Guys" /> Which subsequently caused a citywide power outage and shut down all the safety droids.<ref name="Skeleton Crew Explained" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|The supervisor itself was this giant droid. Then we thought, okay, well how do we do that? How we communicate that visually? And so we thought, okay, well, let's create this giant room with these giant windows, but then at the center of it will have a giant R2 head. Not literally, but that was the idea. The scale of it makes you wonder, okay, what is this supervisor being?|[[Doug Chiang]]|<ref name="Design">{{SWYouTube|-N11lYPwaS4|Star Wars: Skeleton Crew &#124; Behind the Design &#124; Disney+}}</ref>}}
The Supervisor was first mentioned in the [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew]]'' episode "[[This Could Be a Real Adventure]]," which premiered on [[December 2]], [[2024]].<ref name="RealAdventure" /> He was voiced by [[Stephen Fry]] in the episode "[[We're Gonna Be In So Much Trouble]]."<ref name="Trouble" /> His design took inspiration from [[Wikipedia:Byron Haskin|Byron Haskin's]] [[1950s#1953|1953]] film [[Wikipedia:The War of the Worlds (1953 film)|''The War of the Worlds'']] and [[Wikipedia:Victor Fleming|Victor Fleming's]] [[1930s#1939|1939]] film [[Wikipedia:The Wizard of Oz|''The Wizard of Oz'']], as well as the dome shape of [[R2-D2]].<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=season-1-episode-8-trivia-gallery-skeleton-crew|text="The Real Good Guys" Trivia Gallery &#124; Skeleton Crew}} {{C|slide 1}}</ref>

